- `unitAt` returns alive unit; dead token not selectable. fine.
- `pointToCell` uses rect width; canvas CSS size equals view size. good.
- `attack` calls `finishHero` which may auto end turn; but `G.busy=false` before. good.
- `stageWon` called from attack; doesn't reset G.busy but sets phase over and busy true. fine.
- `victory` uses G.runTurns but after final stage win, the last turn isn't counted because endPlayerTurn wasn't called. It counts completed enemy phases. Fine. Maybe show 4+; acceptable.
- `stageClearSheet` sets G.stageIndex = idx+1 before startStage; startStage sets it again. fine.
- `startStage` saves progress before first turn. good.
- `goHome` increments token, sets phase home, closes overlay, shows home. Good.
- `updateHome` loadProgress: if save exists stageIndex valid. Good.
- `askNewRun` when save exists; if user starts new run, old save overwritten by startStage save.
- `openPause` while overlay open? menu button is under overlay, can't click. Escape checks overlay hidden.
- `Sound.unlock` only if not muted; if muted, no context. Toggling unmute calls unlock then play. Good.
- `Sound.tone` uses `this.ctx.currentTime`; if muted, play returns before tone. Good.
- `localStorage` may throw in private mode on getItem? Usually no. loadProgress catches. `Sound.muted` initial `localStorage.getItem` not caught! In some environments (file://) localStorage may throw SecurityError. Add try/catch. Also `MUTE_KEY` access at module init. Let's guard.
